<section class="marketing-section marketing-soft" id="spreadsheet-problems">
  <div class="marketing-section-head">
    <h2>Problems with Spreadsheet-based Quoting</h2>
  </div>
  <p class="seo-summary"><strong>Spreadsheet quoting breaks when export deal volume and revision speed increase.</strong></p>
  <p>Teams lose execution speed because quote updates are spread across files, chats, and email attachments.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Version confusion grows when multiple quote files circulate across teammates.</li>
    <li>Manual updates delay buyer response in fast export negotiations.</li>
    <li>Quote revision control is difficult across email attachment chains.</li>
    <li>Formula and copy errors create direct margin and trust risk.</li>
    <li>Buyer visibility drops when the latest quote is not clearly accessible.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>That is why many teams adopt foreign trade quotation software as a spreadsheet alternative for export teams.</p>
</section>

